# vpsinfra registry entry for the price feed, to be copied to
# projects/leekdefi-feed.env in the infrastructure repo (and generated there
# with scripts/add-project.sh rather than by hand, per docs/adding-projects.md).
#
# Two projects serve one site. The dapp is `leekdefi`, this is its feed, and
# they are separate deployment units because they fail separately: a feed that
# cannot reach its price source must not take the dapp's static assets down
# with it, and rolling one back should not roll back the other.
#
# The dapp reaches this service at a SAME-ORIGIN path. Caddy proxies
# `/prices` on leekdefi.0xoucanproject.xyz to this container over the internal
# network, so the browser makes no cross-origin request and the dapp's
# `connect-src` stays 'self' for prices. That is the whole reason for the
# arrangement: every origin added to a CSP is a place a compromised dependency
# could exfiltrate to.
PROJECT_NAME=leekdefi-feed
# Its own hostname, because vpsinfra treats hostnames as deployment boundaries
# and the health gate validates one. Nothing but /healthz answers on it; see
# the Caddy template beside this file.
HOSTNAME=leekdefi-feed.0xoucanproject.xyz
# Public, because the Buildathon requires a public repository and the history
# has been audited for secrets (see DEPLOYMENT.md, "Before this repository
# goes public"). A public source needs no read-only deploy key on the VPS.
SOURCE_TYPE=github-public
REPOSITORY=git@github.com:0xOucan/leek-stocks.git
BRANCH=main
APP_TYPE=node
CONTAINER_PORT=8787
HEALTH_PATH=/healthz
DATABASE_TYPE=none
DOCKERFILE=feed/deploy/Dockerfile
BUILD_CONTEXT=.
# Node plus viem, publishing a handful of rounds an hour. Measured locally at
# well under 100 MB resident; 192m leaves headroom for a GC spike rather than
# an OOM kill in the middle of a publish.
MEMORY_LIMIT=192m
CPU_LIMIT=0.50
# The process writes nothing: state is the chain and the status is in memory.
READ_ONLY=true
CADDY_TEMPLATE=projects/leekdefi-feed.caddy.tmpl
